# Portfolio Website Project

This is a cloud engineer portfolio website with:
- React frontend (Vite build system)
- Terraform infrastructure for AWS (S3 + CloudFront + Route53 + ACM)
- Docker-based Terraform runner

## Project Structure

```
src/App.jsx          - Main React component with CONFIG and SCRIPTS to customize
terraform/           - AWS infrastructure as code
terraform/bootstrap/ - State backend setup (run first)
run.sh              - Docker commands for Terraform operations
```

## Key Files to Edit

1. `src/App.jsx` - Update CONFIG object with user's details:
   - name, title, github username
   - email, linkedin
   - yearsExperience
   - certifications array
   - skills object

2. `src/App.jsx` - Update SCRIPTS object with user's scripts:
   - powershell array
   - bash array  
   - terraform array

3. `terraform/terraform.tfvars` - Set domain_name for deployment

## Development Commands

```bash
npm install          # Install dependencies
npm run dev          # Start dev server at localhost:5173
npm run build        # Production build to dist/
```

## Deployment Commands (requires Docker)

```bash
./run.sh bootstrap-init   # Initialize state backend
./run.sh bootstrap-apply  # Create S3 + DynamoDB for state
./run.sh init             # Initialize main Terraform
./run.sh plan             # Preview infrastructure changes
./run.sh apply            # Deploy infrastructure
./run.sh build            # Build React app in Docker
./run.sh deploy           # Sync to S3 + invalidate CloudFront
```

## Tech Stack

- React 18 + Vite
- Tailwind-style CSS (custom properties)
- JetBrains Mono + Space Grotesk fonts
- Terraform 1.7+
- AWS: S3, CloudFront, Route53, ACM, DynamoDB
